Android and LineageOS
---------------------
upstream/lineage16/ contains a source snapshot based on Android 9 / LineageOS
16. upstream/lineage16-revisions.xml records the upstream revisions used as
the starting point; it is provenance, not a build or compatibility gate.
Android and LineageOS contain material under several licences, predominantly
Apache-2.0 as well as GPL, LGPL, BSD, MIT, Unicode and other terms. The original
copyright notices, NOTICE and licence files remain with the relevant sources.
Android source and licence information: https://source.android.com/docs/setup/contribute/licenses

upstream/aosp-oreo-system-core/sdcard/ includes Android Open Source Project
source and its Apache-2.0 notice. Other copied or adapted source has its own
notice in system/zx300a/android/{audiohal,exfat,graphics,launcher,storage}/.
In particular, fuse-exfat and libfuse-lite have GPL/LGPL obligations; do not
assume the project-wide MIT licence applies to them.

Additional Android library sources
----------------------------------
The archives in upstream/ also include Apache-2.0 sources used to rebuild
Android libraries: Material Components 1.0.0-alpha1 and its preceding support
design sources (https://github.com/material-components/material-components-android),
the earlier support-design widget implementation from Android support commit
965e46b2ba086625c54aa70de1d853083081e7b0,
the AndroidX versionedparcelable directory at Android support commit
5d2a3088e1b089d2cc776415740540079d5e0529; Slice and compatible Core source
directories from Android support commit 2445931b27bd32831336c1aff7dbd490af8b83d4;
Android ConstraintLayout and its
solver from the studio-3.1.2 sherpa tag
(https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/opt/sherpa/), and
Flexbox Layout 0.3.2 (https://github.com/google/flexbox-layout).
Source notices and the Apache-2.0 licence are retained in the archives. The
archives exclude Gradle wrapper JARs; builders supply the Gradle build tools.

Sony-published open source
--------------------------
upstream/sony-open/ contains source published by Sony for this device family:
the Linux 3.10.26 kernel, BusyBox 1.23.1, glibc 2.23 and ALSA lib 1.0.29.
The kernel and BusyBox distributions include GPL-2.0 material; glibc and ALSA
include LGPL material. Consult the files and licence texts in each archive for
the exact terms and exceptions. Old compiled executables, objects, encoded
firmware images and identified firmware byte arrays embedded in the supplied
kernel and BusyBox source archives were removed. Available source, copyright
and licence notices were retained. Other hardware configurations may need
their own firmware inputs. WalkDroid kernel changes and build scripts are in
system/zx300a/kernel/ and tools/.
Sony source and notices: https://oss.sony.net/Products/Linux/Audio/NW-ZX300G.html

GNU C Library used by the prebuilt release
-----------------------------------------
The release's static BusyBox is linked with Ubuntu GLIBC 2.43-2ubuntu2.
The corresponding upstream source and Ubuntu packaging changes are provided
in upstream/ubuntu-glibc/ under the GNU LGPL and the other notices in that
source. The .dsc is upstream source-package metadata, not a build requirement.
The release includes its BusyBox configuration; the project patch and build
instructions are supplied with the sources. Its original GPL-2.0-only licence
notice and full licence text are included as licenses/BusyBox-LICENSE.txt.
Builders using a different C library must observe that library's own terms.
Source: https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/g/glibc/

GCC runtime used by the prebuilt release
---------------------------------------
Some device components contain statically linked libgcc routines from Ubuntu
GCC 15.2.0-16ubuntu1, supplied by the gcc-15-cross 15ubuntu1 package. The
corresponding GCC upstream source and both Ubuntu packaging source packages are
in upstream/ubuntu-gcc/. The affected libgcc files are under GPL-3.0-or-later
with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1; the release includes the licence
and exception texts. The .dsc files are source-package metadata, not a
requirement for compiling or running the system.
Sources: https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/g/gcc-15/
         https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/g/gcc-15-cross/

The display adapter uses Apache-2.0 interface headers from Android CTS rather
than copying the GPL driver headers into the Apache gralloc component. Its
source provenance and the compared ARM32 ABI are described in
system/zx300a/android/graphics/NOTICE.md. The kernel retains its own GPL and
other applicable notices.

